From e35af7bc1557b5197e7aab989bdd67ddbf9f7a24 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 06:00:39 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] dicts: mint RFW_252 and translate the Warden block-split
 labels

RWDN_73-76 - the Countries / Threat feeds / Manual blocks / Unclassified labels
on Warden's blocked-hits breakdown - were the only keys on that page still
carrying the English string in all 24 non-EN packs. They were minted with the
block split and the translation pass never followed. Invisible as 11px grey
subtext; a band of English now that the breakdown is a strip above the country
table. All 24 filled, IN PLACE at the existing line indices, so the closed
resolver's line-index lockstep is untouched by construction. Colon convention
follows each pack's own habit: fullwidth for CN/TW/JP, ASCII elsewhere, and no
space before it in the ASUS French packs.

RFW_252 ("Both") is appended English to all 25 as usual. It is NOT translated
here on purpose: the other three options in that same select (RFW_100/138/139)
are English in every non-EN pack, as is the whole RFW_* namespace, so
translating one option alone would render "None / Drop / Accept / Beide". The
namespace-wide gap is tracked in the backlog. Reusing ASUS's own
option_both_direction was considered and rejected - it is translated 24/24 but
means "bidirectional" (CN renders it as such), and this select is a
logged-packets type, not a direction.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
